            <ArticleTitle>Hyperplasia and Hypertrophy of Pacinian Corpuscles: A Case Report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e100-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/DAD.0000000000000162</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The proliferation of Pacinian corpuscles is a rare benign lesion that occurs frequently in the fingers of hands, with the only clinical sign of pain when a drastic temperature change happens. A case of an extremely rare lesion in which we observed hypertrophy and hyperplasia of Pacinian corpuscles has been reported.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
